    <statement><p>Find the differential <m>df</m> of the function <m>f</m>
given the gradient.
<me>\nabla f =  \left(4x+2e^{-y}\right)\boldsymbol{i}+2xe^{-y}\boldsymbol{j}.</me></p>
<p><m>df =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(4x+2e^{-y}\right)dx+2xe^{-y}dy</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\nabla f = f_x \mathbf{i} + f_y \mathbf{j}</m> and
<m>df = f_x\, dx + f_yd\, y</m>, we have
<me>df = \left(4x+2e^{-y}\right)dx+2xe^{-y}dy.</me>



</solution>
